text:
The sea, that calls you so, and smiles;

 The sea with her hands to beckon ;

 Whence she has taken away your sins,

 And left you but your sorrows alone !

"Through golden beams, I enter;
The stately stair, resplendent;
A glorious feast at length is near."

O’er all the land, through many an isle and bay,
 The morning winds are calling to the sea;

 And the white billows softly heave away
 To where their mothers wait them by the shore,
 With arms outstretched that kiss them as they come,
 Where every wave is kindled into song;

 For ever on the morning breezes blow
 A soft sweet note that wakens up life’s day;
 So from each heart this music shall be sent,
 As we go forth with hands uplifted to pray.

Oh no! Oh no! My poor little head is aching;
It seems to say that I've not done enough praying;
I'll have to go to church tonight, instead of playing;
A-worrying on me now do you see it all?
But what does this mean? Is it because they pray?

And now, O mighty God! we trust thee
For thine own mercies' sake to pardon us;

We know that Thou hast power above us ;
In grace Thy judgments are as high as Thou !
